.TH "PERCH-ACCOUNT" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-account \- add, list, password, disable, or enable accounts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch account [OPTIONS] COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Manage local mailbox accounts. Creating an account also creates the default mailbox set: INBOX, Sent, Drafts, Trash, Junk, and Archive.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Passwords are hashed with Argon2id.
.IP \(bu 2
Account changes are written to SQLite and apply without restarting serve.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add
create an account
.TP
.B list
list accounts
.TP
.B passwd
change an account password
.TP
.B disable
disable an account
.TP
.B enable
enable an account
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch account add \-\-email you@example.com

perch account list

perch account passwd \-\-email you@example.com
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\-add\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\-disable\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\-enable\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\-list\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\-passwd\fR(1)
